@prefix : <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix elite: <https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#> .

<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo/neo> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                        owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo/0.0.1/neo> ;
                                        owl:imports <https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite> ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Anna Anchini"@it ,
                                                                               "Cristiana Tropeano"@it ,
                                                                               "Dario Rimondini"@it ,
                                                                               "Francesca Venturi"@it ,
                                                                               "Francesco Antonio Zaccarini"@it ,
                                                                               "Giovanna Casula"@it ,
                                                                               "Ilaria Maria Paponetti"@it ,
                                                                               "Nicola Ferro"@it ,
                                                                               "Samuele Baldini"@it ,
                                                                               "Saverio Quaranta"@it ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Emanuele Ghedini"@it ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> """The Nuclear Energy Ontology (NEO) is a domain ontology developed under the EMMO framework for the representation of concepts in the field of nuclear energy. It is based on commonly used standardization vocabularies, such as:
    - ISO 12749 - Nuclear energy, nuclear technologies, and radiological protection
    - \"Construction Technologies for Nuclear Power Plants\", IAEA Nuclear Energy Series, No. NP-T-2.5, IAEA, Vienna (AU), 2011
    - IAEA Safety Glossary, Terminology Used in Nuclear Safety and Radiation Protection, 2018 Edition.
    - Nuclear Regulatory Commission reports and documents.
    - Official U.S. federal regulations database, maintained by the National Archives.

It includes the representation of the Fukushima Daichi accident, based on the official IAEA report: \"The Fukushima Daiichi accident - Technical Volume 1: Description and Context of the Accident\", IAEA, Vienna (AU), 2015, STI/PUB/1710, ISBN 978–92–0–107015–9

The ontology is still in development phase and provides a partial cover of the nuclear engineering domain and Fukushima Daichi accident report."""@en ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Nuclear Energy Ontology"@en .

