<http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/description
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/license
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/title
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment
rdfs:comment rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:label .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:label .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isOutputOf
elite:isOutputOf rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf elite:partakesIn .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV
:R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "definition"@en ;
                         :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV "A short explanation aimed to guide the reader towards the intended interpretation of the ontological concept."@en ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:comment .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#R9Q7fCgWnAkzqnVMtRJ4WDv
:R9Q7fCgWnAkzqnVMtRJ4WDv rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "example"@en ;
                         :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV "A reference to real entities aimed to explain the intended interpretation for the ontological concept."@en ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:comment .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#RR3uD2d7YfhHohfv2Nm6sX
:RR3uD2d7YfhHohfv2Nm6sX rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "comment"@en ;
                        :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV "Additional text aimed to explain the conceptual choices of the authors."@en ;
                        rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:comment .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#referenceARIS
:referenceARIS rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
               rdfs:comment "Reference to the IAEA Advanced Reactor Information System Glossary."@en ;
               rdfs:seeAlso <https://aris.iaea.org/Glossary/> ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ARIS Reference"@en ;
               rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
               rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#referenceINIS
:referenceINIS rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
               rdfs:comment "Reference to the IAEA INIS Thesaurus term."@en ;
               rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.iaea.org/resources/databases/inis/thesaurus> ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "INIS Reference"@en ;
               rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
               rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#referenceISO
:referenceISO rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
              rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#home> ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ISO Reference"@en ;
              rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
              rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#referenceNRC
:referenceNRC rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
              rdfs:comment "This is the direct reference to the Nuclear Regulatory Commission Glossary" ;
              rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.nrc.gov/reading-rm/basic-ref/glossary> ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NRCG Reference"@en ;
              rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
              rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#referenceNSSG
:referenceNSSG rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
               rdfs:comment "Reference to IAEA Nuclear Safety and Security Glossary term IRI."@en ;
               rdfs:seeAlso <https://vocabulary.iaea.org/iaea-safety-glossary.html> ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NSSG Reference"@en ;
               rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
               rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo/neo#NRC_Reference
:NRC_Reference rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
               rdfs:comment "This is the link to any Nuclear Regulatory Commission document/report."@en ;
               rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
               rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo/neo#eCFR_Reference
:eCFR_Reference rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                rdfs:comment "Official U.S. federal regulations database, maintained by the National Archives." ;
                :eCFR_Reference ""^^xsd:anyURI ;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
                rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#affects
elite:affects rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#foregoes
elite:foregoes rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#hasBehaviour
elite:hasBehaviour rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isBehaviourOf
elite:isBehaviourOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isConstituentOf
elite:isConstituentOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isConstitutiveProcessOf
elite:isConstitutiveProcessOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isInputOf
elite:isInputOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isParticipantOf
elite:isParticipantOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isStageOf
elite:isStageOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#isSubProcessOf
elite:isSubProcessOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/0.0.7/elite#participatesTo
elite:participatesTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#RB4rNlczhggIx7lqdEK2d9c
:RB4rNlczhggIx7lqdEK2d9c rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf elite:isConstituentOf ;
                         rdfs:comment "Defines the position of an object in a Nuclear Power Plant."@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The spatial relation  between an entity and another the entity that contains it."@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "isContainedBy"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#RBbSkE1mWA7Oq2RnEiKiOzM
:RBbSkE1mWA7Oq2RnEiKiOzM rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain :RDZtzLsQmngV2BtJvmS5pbg ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "It relates the Nuclear Power Plant Workers to the place where they can enter, following safety requirements"@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "CanAccessIn"@en .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#ArtificialRadioactiveMaterial
:ArtificialRadioactiveMaterial rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf :RadioactiveMaterialByOccurrence ;
                               owl:disjointWith :NaturallyRadioactiveMaterial .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#BoratedWaterInjectionSystem
:BoratedWaterInjectionSystem rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf :WaterInjectionSystem ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty elite:partakesIn ;
                                               owl:someValuesFrom :ReactorMitigationCoolingSystem
                                             ] ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty elite:participatesTo ;
                                               owl:someValuesFrom :SafetySystem
                                             ] ;
                             rdfs:label "BoratedWaterInjectionSystem" ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment> "Borated water injection system is a system which injects borated water to cool down the reactor core" .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#InjectedMaterial
:InjectedMaterial rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearEnergyObject ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "SuppliedMaterial" ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Material used for material supplying" ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "InjectedMaterial"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :InjectedMaterial ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Material used for material supplying" ;
   rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:14452:ed-1:v1:en:term:2.40"
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearEnergyObject
:NuclearEnergyObject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/hume#Object> ;
                     rdfs:comment "Nuclear energy is a form of heat energy that can be released via reactions involving nuclear fusion or fission taking place between neutrons and protons in the nucleus of an atom. Electricity can be produced when a large amount of heat energy released is applied to generate steam from turbines (Fig. 1.4). Uranium-235, an isotope of uranium, is the most commonly used element in industrial nuclear power generators." ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "NuclearDomainObject" ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#comment> "It misses the nuclear energy research" ,
                                                                   "nuclear related energy object and people" ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "It is an object involved in the nuclear energy production, management and control." ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NuclearEnergyObject"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NuclearEnergyObject ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:comment ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Nuclear energy is a form of heat energy that can be released via reactions involving nuclear fusion or fission taking place between neutrons and protons in the nucleus of an atom. Electricity can be produced when a large amount of heat energy released is applied to generate steam from turbines (Fig. 1.4). Uranium-235, an isotope of uranium, is the most commonly used element in industrial nuclear power generators." ;
   rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/nuclear-energy"
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearEnergyProcess
:NuclearEnergyProcess rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/hume#Process> .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearEnergyRole
:NuclearEnergyRole rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/hume#Role> ;
                   rdfs:label "NuclearEnergyRole"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearPowerReactor
:NuclearPowerReactor rdf:type owl:Class ;
                     rdfs:subClassOf :Nuclear_Reactor ,
                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                       owl:onProperty elite:isConstituentOf ;
                                       owl:someValuesFrom :NuclearPowerPlant
                                     ] ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NuclearPowerReactor"@en ;
                     :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV "nuclear reactor (3.1.22) conceived to produce electrical power" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NuclearPowerReactor ;
   owl:annotatedProperty :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "nuclear reactor (3.1.22) conceived to produce electrical power" ;
   :referenceISO <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:12749:-5:ed-1:v1:en:term:3.2.1.1>
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#Nuclear_Reactor
:Nuclear_Reactor rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearEnergyObject ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Nuclear Reactor"@en ;
                :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV "special device having an inventory of nuclear fuel material containing fissionable nuclides (3.1.2) and often neutron moderating, neutron absorbing and cooling materials, all of them geometrically arranged in a particular neutron multiplicative configuration (3.1.10) designed and built for having the capability of initiating, maintaining and extinguishing a controlled, self-sustaining nuclear fission (3.1.1) chain reaction, under adequate safety conditions" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :Nuclear_Reactor ;
   owl:annotatedProperty :R8xx0dhbEh1tjGMDwNZfckV ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "special device having an inventory of nuclear fuel material containing fissionable nuclides (3.1.2) and often neutron moderating, neutron absorbing and cooling materials, all of them geometrically arranged in a particular neutron multiplicative configuration (3.1.10) designed and built for having the capability of initiating, maintaining and extinguishing a controlled, self-sustaining nuclear fission (3.1.1) chain reaction, under adequate safety conditions" ;
   :referenceISO <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:12749:-5:ed-1:v1:en:term:3.1.22>
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearPowerPlant
:NuclearPowerPlant rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearEnergyObject ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty elite:participatesTo ;
                                          owl:someValuesFrom :NPPOperationManagement
                                        ] ;
                        rdfs:comment "Nuclear power plant is a nuclear reactor or reactors together with all structures, systems and components necessary for safety and for the production of power, i.e. heat or electricity (ISO 12749-5:2018)."@en ;
                        rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_power_plant> ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "NPP"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A nuclear reactor installation that produces electrical and/or heat energy (ISO 12749-5:2018)."@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NuclearPowerPlant"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NuclearPowerPlant ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "A nuclear reactor installation that produces electrical and/or heat energy (ISO 12749-5:2018)."@en ;
   :referenceISO <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:12749:-5:ed-1:v1:en:term:3.2.5>
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#ContainmentBuilding
:ContainmentBuilding rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearPowerPlantBuilding ;
                        rdfs:comment "On the IAEA report is called \"reactor building\""@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ReactorBuilding"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A hermetically sealed building which houses the nuclear reactor core and other systems that could potentially release fission products to the atmosphere during an accident."@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ContainmentBuilding"@en ;
                        :referenceARIS "Contaiment Building"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NPPShutdown
:NPPShutdown rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :NPPNormalOperation ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shutdown is the state of a nuclear reactor when the fission reaction is slowed significantly or halted completely"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NPPShutdown"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NPPShutdown ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Shutdown is the state of a nuclear reactor when the fission reaction is slowed significantly or halted completely"@en ;
   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shutdown>
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearInelasticScattering
:NuclearInelasticScattering rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearReaction ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty elite:isSubProcessOf ;
                                          owl:someValuesFrom :ReactorCoreEnergyProduction
                                        ] ;
                        rdfs:comment """electron scattering in which energy and/or momentum are not conserved in the collision system
Note 1 to entry: For inelastic scattering, the electron trajectory is modified by plasmon loss, core loss, and other multiple scatterings"""@en ;
                        rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:15932:ed-1:v1:en:term:2.2.2> ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """When the compound nucleus formed by neutron capture decays by the emission of
one neutron, leaving the nucleus in an excited state which subsequently undergoes
further decays, the event is referred to as inelastic scattering."""@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NuclearInelasticScattering"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NuclearInelasticScattering ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:15932:ed-1:v1:en:term:2.2.2> ;
   :referenceISO <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo>
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :NuclearInelasticScattering ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget """When the compound nucleus formed by neutron capture decays by the emission of
one neutron, leaving the nucleus in an excited state which subsequently undergoes
further decays, the event is referred to as inelastic scattering."""@en ;
   rdfs:isDefinedBy "Stacey, W. (2018). Nuclear Reactor Physics (3rd ed.). Wiley. Retrieved from https://www.perlego.com/book/993700/nuclear-reactor-physics-pdf (Original work published 2018)"
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#AutomaticReactorDepressurization
:AutomaticReactorDepressurization rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :AOOControl ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty elite:affects ;
                                          owl:someValuesFrom :LowPressureEmergencyCoreCoolingSystems
                                        ] ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rapidly lower reactor pressure to allow low pressure injection sources to maintain reactor water level above the Top of Active Fuel."@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "AutomaticReactorDepressurization"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :AutomaticReactorDepressurization ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Rapidly lower reactor pressure to allow low pressure injection sources to maintain reactor water level above the Top of Active Fuel."@en ;
   :referenceNRC "https://www.nrc.gov/docs/ML1125/ML11258A366.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#MakeUpWaterCondensateSystem
:MakeUpWaterCondensateSystem rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :ReactorBuildingContents ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty :RB4rNlczhggIx7lqdEK2d9c ;
                                          owl:someValuesFrom :ContainmentBuilding
                                        ] ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "MUWC"@en ,
                                                                       "ReactorMakeUpWaterCondensateSystem"@en ,
                                                                       "ReactorWaterCleanupSystem"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The purpose of the reactor water cleanup system (RWCU) is to maintain a high reactor water quality by removing fission products, corrosion products, and other soluble and insoluble impurities. The reactor water cleanup pump takes water from the recirculation system and the vessel bottom head and pumps the water through heat exchangers to cool the flow. The water is then sent through filter/demineralizers for cleanup. After cleanup, the water is returned to the reactor vessel via the feedwater piping."@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "MakeUpWaterCondensateSystem"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :MakeUpWaterCondensateSystem ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "The purpose of the reactor water cleanup system (RWCU) is to maintain a high reactor water quality by removing fission products, corrosion products, and other soluble and insoluble impurities. The reactor water cleanup pump takes water from the recirculation system and the vessel bottom head and pumps the water through heat exchangers to cool the flow. The water is then sent through filter/demineralizers for cleanup. After cleanup, the water is returned to the reactor vessel via the feedwater piping."@en ;
   :referenceNRC <https://www.nrc.gov/docs/ML1209/ML120970422.pdf>
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#ProtectiveSeparation
:ProtectiveSeparation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :NPPProtection ;
                        rdfs:comment """Se mettiamo un processo tipo separazione o scollegamento possiamo poi creare una relazione \"from\" turbine.
Tipo protective  separation
electrically protective  separation
separation of one electric circuit from another by means of:
— double insulation  (3.4.8); or
— basic insulation  (3.4.6) and electrically protective screening (shielding); or
— reinforced insulation  (3.4.9)
[SOURCE: IEC 61140:2016, 3.24]
ISO 18246:2023(en), 3.4.12"""@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "MainLineSeparation" ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ProtectiveSeparation"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#ReactorProtectionSystem
:ReactorProtectionSystem rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :SafetySystem ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "RPS"@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """System that monitors the operation (3.9.1) of a reactor and which, on sensing an abnormal condition, automatically initiates actions to prevent an unsafe or potentially unsafe condition 

Note 1 to entry: This use of the term protection refers to protection of the plant; the system in this case encompasses all electrical and mechanical devices and circuitry, from sensors to actuation device input terminals. 

Note 2 to entry: The reactor protection system (RPS) provides protection against abnormal conditions such as reactor over-power, too fast neutron (3.1.5.1) flux increase, high reactor inlet temperature, primary heat transport system (3.7.2.5) over-pressure, etc. 

Note 3 to entry: The reactor protection system (RPS) imposes actions on several systems, especially, the reactor regulation system (3.7.2.1.2) (RRS), the reactor shutdown system (3.8.16.1) (SDS) and the emergency core cooling system (3.8.16.2) (ECCS). ﻿"""@en ;
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ReactorProtectionSystem"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :ReactorProtectionSystem ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget """System that monitors the operation (3.9.1) of a reactor and which, on sensing an abnormal condition, automatically initiates actions to prevent an unsafe or potentially unsafe condition 

Note 1 to entry: This use of the term protection refers to protection of the plant; the system in this case encompasses all electrical and mechanical devices and circuitry, from sensors to actuation device input terminals. 

Note 2 to entry: The reactor protection system (RPS) provides protection against abnormal conditions such as reactor over-power, too fast neutron (3.1.5.1) flux increase, high reactor inlet temperature, primary heat transport system (3.7.2.5) over-pressure, etc. 

Note 3 to entry: The reactor protection system (RPS) imposes actions on several systems, especially, the reactor regulation system (3.7.2.1.2) (RRS), the reactor shutdown system (3.8.16.1) (SDS) and the emergency core cooling system (3.8.16.2) (ECCS). ﻿"""@en ;
   :referenceISO """https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:12749:-5:ed-1:v1:en
Nuclear energy, nuclear technologies, and radiological protection — Vocabulary — Part 5: Nuclear reactors
ISO 12749-5:2018(en)"""^^xsd:anyURI
 ] .


