###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#IsolationCondenserTank
:IsolationCondenserTank rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :ReactorBuildingContents ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty elite:isConstituentOf ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom :IsolationCondenserSystem
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:comment "In the Unit 1 design, there were two separate and redundant isolation condenser loops. In these closed loops, the primary side of the isolation condenser received steam generated in the reactor and condensed it by cooling inside the heat exchanger tubes that were submerged in colder water tanks (isolation condenser pools) located outside the primary containment vessel."@en ;
                         rdfs:seeAlso """Box 1.1–2. Systems for cooling the core when the reactor is isolated from the turbines. The Fukushima Daiichi Accident Technical Volume 1/5 
link: https://www-pub.iaea.org/MTCD/Publications/PDF/AdditionalVolumes/P1710/Pub1710-TV1-Web.pdf"""@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "IsolatioCondenserPool"@en ,
                                                                        "ReactorIsolationCondenserTank"@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "IsolationCondenserTank"@en .


