###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#NuclearElasticScattering
:NuclearElasticScattering rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :NuclearReaction ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty elite:isSubProcessOf ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom :ReactorCoreEnergyProduction
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:comment """collision between a moving particle and a second particle in which the total kinetic energy (3.35) and the total momentum are conserved
Note 1 to entry: See inelastic scattering (4.2).
Note 2 to entry: In elastic scattering interactions, the moving particle can be deflected through angles of up to 180°."""@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "BinaryElasticScattering" ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "collision between a neutron and a nucleus in which the total kinetic energy (3.35) and the total momentum are conserved"@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NuclearElasticScattering"@en .


