   owl:annotatedTarget "equipment in a steam turbine BOP (3.4.1.3), aimed at receiving the exhausting low-pressure turbine steam, bringing this fluid into the liquid state by massive cooling "@en ;
   :referenceISO "ISO 12749-5:2018(en)  Nuclear energy, nuclear technologies, and radiological protection — Vocabulary — Part 5: Nuclear reactors "^^xsd:anyURI
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/neo#RHROperation
:RHROperation rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :NPPNormalOperation ;
                         rdfs:comment """Residual heat transfer systems include systems designed to transfer heat from the residual heat removal systems to the ultimate heat sink.
 The capabilities to discharge residual heat to the ultimate heat sink are based on at least one heat sink and one heat transfer chain always being available for the different shutdown conditions."""@en ;
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "RHROperation"@en .


