                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An explosion is a sudden catastrophic release of energy, causing a pressure wave. An explosion happens when a free gas expands very quickly, because of a chemical reaction that produces a gas, or because a container of pressurized gas ruptures."@en ;
